Solaris DLPI inline regression test
----------------------------------

Use two isolated Ethernet segments joined only by the Suricata DLPI workers.
Keep management on a separate link. The virtual switch must permit the remote
endpoint MAC addresses and VLAN 42; a ping alone does not validate this setup.
The probes use source addresses 198.18.0.1 and 2001:db8:42::1, in both
directions. Any endpoint anti-spoof policy must permit those test addresses.
An untagged zone VNIC may filter VLAN frames before Suricata receives them;
use VLAN-capable links or isolated virtual Ethernet pairs for the full test.
Run the probe as root (raw DLPI privileges) on each endpoint, with Python 3.
Read the script from the Userland workspace, or stream it to Python on stdin;
it needs no third-party modules and creates no files.

First check frame construction, without network access:

  python3 -B tests/dlpi-frames.py selftest --token selftest

On the receiving endpoint (replace MAC addresses with the actual endpoint
addresses; do not use a management link):

  python3 -B tests/dlpi-frames.py receive --link net1 \
    --src 02:00:00:00:00:01 --dst 02:00:00:00:00:02 \
    --token unique-test-1 --repeat 3 --seconds 60 --expect all

Wait for the JSON "ready" event, then on the sending endpoint:

  python3 -B tests/dlpi-frames.py send --link net1 \
    --src 02:00:00:00:00:01 --dst 02:00:00:00:00:02 \
    --token unique-test-1 --repeat 3

The receiver expects exactly three byte-identical frames of each type: ARP,
IPv4/ICMP, IPv6/ICMPv6, VLAN-42 IPv4, VLAN-42 IPv6, and experimental EtherType
0x88b5. It fails on missing frames, modified bytes, or duplicate forwarding.
Use a new token per run, swap the endpoint MACs, and repeat in the reverse
direction. Every successful probe returns zero and prints result=PASS.

Repeat with these Suricata rules and receiver --expect drop-ip:

  drop icmp any any -> any any (msg:"DLPI IPv4 drop"; sid:9900101; rev:1;)
  drop icmpv6 any any -> any any (msg:"DLPI IPv6 drop"; sid:9900102; rev:1;)

Only ARP and experimental frames must arrive; tagged and untagged IPv4/IPv6
must be blocked. Check the corresponding alerts, decoder VLAN/IPv6 counters,
and capture.dlpi_send_errors. Repeat with Suricata stopped and --expect none
to prove that the topology has no bypass path. Save probe output and engine
logs in the task evidence directory inside the Userland workspace.

This is a raw frame forwarding/verdict test, not a complete IPv6 stack,
neighbor-discovery, fragmentation, TCP reassembly, or throughput test.
